# act runs the workflow locally. These flags give the runner what the job needs.
# The Docker daemon socket lets the build job build images and lets the deploy
# job drive kind. The cluster is reached over the host-published API port (see
# the mounted kubeconfig), NOT by joining the kind network: joining it would
# detach the job from act's own service network and break the postgres service.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
--container-daemon-socket /var/run/docker.sock
